---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: "Get the WhereTo App — iOS & Android"
description: "Download WhereTo for iPhone and Android, for trips departing from US airports. Free to download, no subscription, and no in-app ads."
permalink: /app/
---
{#
  The download page: what the app is, the two official store badges, and the
  no-ads promise. Everything else on the site points here. The badges are the
  files in /StoreBadges/, shown as published (don't recolor or crop them).
  /get-app/ is the device-aware version that partner links land on.
#}
<style>
  .app-hero { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 72px 24px 88px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.1fr .9fr; gap: 56px; align-items: center; }
  .app-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(38px, 5vw, 60px); line-height: 1.1; }
  .app-hero h1 em { color: var(--azure); }
  .app-lede { margin-top: 20px; font-size: 19px; max-width: 30em; }
  .app-facts { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px 22px; margin-top: 22px; font-size: 15px; color: var(--wg600); }
  .app-facts b { color: var(--navy); font-weight: 600; }
  .app-badges { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 14px; margin-top: 26px; }
  .app-badges .store-badge[hidden] { display: none; } /* the badge rule sets display, which would otherwise beat [hidden] */
  .app-art { display: flex; justify-content: center; }
  .app-art img { width: 100%; max-width: 400px; height: auto; }

  .noads { background: var(--wg100); padding: 64px 24px; text-align: center; }
  .noads-in { max-width: 1080px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .noads h2 { font-size: clamp(32px, 4vw, 46px); line-height: 1.15; }
  .noads-lede { max-width: 40em; margin: 16px auto 0; font-size: 18px; }
  .noads-pts { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 24px; margin-top: 38px; text-align: left; }
  .noads-pts h3 { font-weight: 700; font-size: 20px; line-height: 1.3; margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .noads-pts p { font-size: 15.5px; line-height: 1.65; }
  .noads-link { display: inline-block; margin-top: 30px; color: var(--azure); font-weight: 600; font-size: 15px; }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .app-hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; padding-top: 40px; gap: 32px; text-align: center; }
    .app-lede { margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; }
    .app-badges, .app-facts { justify-content: center; }
    .app-art { order: -1; }
    .app-art img { max-width: 260px; }
    .noads-pts { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 22px; }
  }
</style>

<main>
  <section class="app-hero">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Free on iPhone and Android</span>
      <h1>Where will your vibes <em>take you?</em></h1>
      <p class="app-lede">Tell WhereTo your budget, dates, and what you want to do. It finds the destinations that fit, then books your flights and hotels in the same app.</p>

      <div class="app-facts">
        <span><b>Free</b> to download, no subscription</span>
        <span><b>US departures</b> to destinations worldwide</span>
      </div>

      <div class="app-badges">
        <a class="store-badge store-badge-apple" data-store="apple" href="{{ site.store.appleHref }}"><img src="/StoreBadges/app-store-badge-black.svg" alt="Download on the App Store" height="54" /></a>
        <a class="store-badge store-badge-google" data-store="google" href="{{ site.store.googleHref }}"><img src="/StoreBadges/google-play-badge.png" alt="Get it on Google Play" height="80" /></a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="app-art"><img src="/media/oniPhone_2.png" alt="The WhereTo app on a phone" width="400" /></div>
  </section>

  <section class="noads">
    <div class="noads-in">
      <span class="eyebrow">Our promise</span>
      <h2>No in-app ads</h2>
      <p class="noads-lede">The only things you'll see in WhereTo are your potential destinations. No banners, no sponsored results, and no full-screen ad to close before you can pick a hotel. We don't serve Google ads or Amazon ads, and we never will.</p>
      <div class="noads-pts">
        <div><h3>Nobody pays to move up your list</h3><p>No hotel and no airline buys a higher spot. The order you see is the order the Vibe Engine scored, based on your budget and your vibes.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Your information is not for sale</h3><p>We don't sell your personal information, and we don't hand it to anyone for their own marketing.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Your trip gets all the attention</h3><p>Your destinations, your flights, your hotels. Nothing else is competing for your attention.</p></div>
      </div>
      <a class="noads-link" href="/legal/privacy/">Read our Privacy Statement</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

<script>
  /* Phones see only their own store's badge. Both badges are in the page, so a
     computer, a tablet, a crawler or a browser without scripts still sees both;
     this only hides the one that does not apply. Same test as /get-app/. */
  (function () {
    var ua = navigator.userAgent || '';
    var ios = /iPhone|iPod/i.test(ua);
    var android = /Android/i.test(ua) && /Mobile/i.test(ua);
    var hide = ios ? 'google' : android ? 'apple' : '';
    if (!hide) return;
    var el = document.querySelector('.app-badges [data-store="' + hide + '"]');
    if (el) el.hidden = true;
  })();
</script>
